---
import CodeFromFile from '../CodeFromFile.astro';
import {machines,codeVersions,sourceRoot,sourceRevision,sampleBase,type Machine} from '../../data/pattern-code';
import {prototypeRoot} from '../../data/pattern-techniques';
interface Props {slug:string;machine:Machine}
const {slug,machine}=Astro.props;
const version=codeVersions[machine];
const selected=machines.find(m=>m.id===machine)!;
const pursuit=slug==='choose-a-target';
const path=pursuit?'commodore-64/patterns/assembly/ai/local-turn/local-turn.inc':slug==='read-input'?version.read:slug==='detect-presses'?version.presses:version.sound;
const lang=machine==='commodore-amiga'?'m68k':machine==='sinclair-zx-spectrum'?'z80':'6502';
const readme=pursuit?'commodore-64/patterns/assembly/ai/local-turn':sampleBase(machine);
---
<section class="technique-code" aria-labelledby="implementation-heading">
 <div class="code-intro"><h2 id="implementation-heading">{selected.name} · {selected.cpu}</h2><p>{pursuit?'Choose a destination, then select the nearest legal neighbouring tile. These are two callable 6502 routines on an original board; they use no hardware registers.':version.result}</p></div>
 <div class="code-and-contract">
  <div class="routine-listing"><h3>{pursuit?'The reusable routines':slug==='read-input'?'Read and store the controls':slug==='detect-presses'?'Keep held state; find new presses':'Start and stop the sound'}</h3>
   <CodeFromFile src={path} lang={lang}/>
   <p class="code-source"><a href={sourceRoot+path}>Open the maintained source file</a> · <a href={sourceRoot.replace('/blob/','/tree/')+readme}>Get the files and build instructions</a></p>
  </div>
  <aside class="caller-contract" aria-label="Calling contract"><h3>Use it in your project</h3>
   {pursuit?<><h4>Before calling</h4><p>Store actor_x/actor_y and player_x/player_y as board coordinates: x=0–8, y=0–6. Set target_mode to 0 for the player’s tile, or 1 for two tiles ahead (Up). Keep the variables and board in writable RAM.</p><h4>Call and read</h4><p>Call choose_target, then choose_turn. Read choice: 0=Up, 1=Left, 2=Down, 3=Right, $FF=no legal neighbour. The routine chooses; the caller decides when to move.</p><h4>What changes</h4><p>A, X, Y, flags, the target and candidate state change. The actor position does not. Squares are small enough that the sum of squared distances fits in one byte.</p><h4>Limits</h4><p>Ties use Up, Left, Down, Right. Reversal is allowed. This local choice can revisit tiles; it does not find a whole route or recreate Pac-Man’s ghosts.</p></>:<><h4>Initialise once</h4><p>{version.init}</p><h4>Call once per update</h4><p>{version.update}</p><h4>State and ownership</h4><p>{version.owns}</p><h4>Timing and sound</h4><p>{version.timing}</p></>}
  </aside>
 </div>
 <section class="integration-example" aria-labelledby="integration-heading"><h2 id="integration-heading">{pursuit?'Let your game apply the turn':'Fit the pieces together'}</h2>
  {pursuit?<><p>Choose a target when the opponent needs a new decision. This caller applies exactly one selected tile step. Keep movement timing and collision policy in the game.</p><CodeFromFile src="commodore-64/patterns/assembly/ai/local-turn/use.inc" lang="6502"/></>:<><p>{machine==='commodore-64'?'This is a complete PAL C64 program: load it, type RUN, and press Fire on joystick port 2. Each new press changes the border and starts one note. Holding Fire does not restart it. Reset to leave.':'This integration fragment belongs inside your own machine’s startup and update loop. It shows every call between the reader, press detector and sound driver; the source folder also provides a complete launchable demo. The fragment itself is not startup code.'}</p>
  <CodeFromFile src={version.usage} lang={lang}/>
  <ol class="integration-steps"><li><strong>Keep the files together.</strong> {machine==='commodore-64'?'Clone the samples repository and keep the relative include paths. The demo reuses joystick.inc and sid-note.inc from their existing pattern folders.':'Copy the reader, presses and caller files, plus the named sound driver, into your program. Include each file once, and adjust include paths to your folder layout.'}</li><li><strong>Set up the machine and state.</strong> Follow the caller’s ownership contract before initialisation. Keep variables in writable memory; reserve the required sound resource.</li><li><strong>Use the two input results for different jobs.</strong> <code>{version.held}</code> says what is held. <code>{version.fresh}</code> says what changed to pressed. This caller tests <code>{version.fire}</code> for its sound action.</li></ol>
  </>}
  {!pursuit&&machine!=='commodore-64'&&<details><summary>Build and run the complete example</summary><p>{version.run}</p><p><a href={`https://github.com/code198x/code-samples/archive/${sourceRevision}.zip`}>Download the matching source revision</a>. From its extracted repository, run <code>make -C {sampleBase(machine)}</code>. Keep the relative include paths; the source folder links above include the Makefile and instructions.</p><CodeFromFile src={version.demo} lang={lang}/></details>}
  <p class="execution-evidence"><strong>What has run:</strong> {pursuit?'The assembled 6502 routine was executed in VICE on all 29 open actor tiles against both target rules: 58 choices compared with an independent calculation. This checks the stated board and choices; it is not historical AI or original-hardware evidence.':version.evidence} <a href={sourceRoot+(pursuit?'scripts/evidence/pattern-library-prototype.json':version.evidenceRecord)}>Read the verification record</a>.</p>
 </section>
</section>
